391	 * AddStorage.tsx used to hold its OWN `MS_PER_AVG_MONTH` and its own inline
392	 * remaining-term expression, so this file reproduced that formula a third time and
393	 * a tripwire kept the copy honest. Both are gone: the component now imports
394	 * `extraDiskProrateCents` (lib/extra-disk.ts) and `remainingMonths`
395	 * (lib/proration.ts) — the same two functions `diskExpandQuote` charges through —
396	 * exactly as ResizePicker already imports `prorateUpgradeCents`.
397	 *
398	 * That matters here more than almost anywhere: this is the figure the customer
399	 * reads and consents to in the confirm dialog, BEFORE the money moves. So the
400	 * assertions below no longer reproduce arithmetic — they assert the component
401	 * cannot derive it at all.
